  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Andrew Eldritch Is Moving Back to Leeds** (1 other source): The uploader suggests listening specifically for this particular track [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **No More Tears**: rare: 8 archived performances [3]\n- **Hebrews 11 40**: rare: 13 archived performances [3]\n- **Younger into**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Andrew Eldritch Is Moving Back to Leeds**: back after 34 archived shows (537 days) [3]\n- **Source Decay**: back after 48 archived shows (731 days) [3]\n- **Matts piano solo**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **Tianchi Lake**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **Doc Gooden**: rare: 13 archived performances [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2019-11-16** (recommended): source not stated; 25 songs; 113 min [1]. Said about its sound: The audio is described as very listenable by the reviewer; Quality is okay, but the microphone gets bumped frequently [1][2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: Andrew Eldritch Is Moving Back to Leeds, Doc Gooden, Hebrews 11 40, No Children, No More Tears, Palmcorder Yajna, Source Decay, Southwestern Territory, Transcendental Youth [1]\n- The recording appears to be missing the twenty-third track [2]\n- This was the first night of a two-date Leeds run [1]",
